    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0227" n="221" xml:id="pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt (Kirk) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-30T17:00:00+02:00">November 30,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 1—12:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2110. My 2071, November 24, 10 a.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d228-f1"/> According
                    British Naval Liaison Head in Cairo it seemed possible French Fleet in
                    Alexandria might come over following Toulon affair<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d228-f2"/> but when Godefroy consulted his captains he found
                    opinions divided and nothing materialized. There was also idea of making for
                    Dakar but that abandoned owing rallying West Africa to Darlan and letter
                    recently addressed to Godefroy by Darlan asking fleet to join him said to have
                    made Godefroy even more obdurate since he professes to regard Darlan “arch
                    traitor”.</p>
                <p>Same source states situation now is that Godefroy still pondering matter with
                    little prospect of doing anything, but British increasingly dissatisfied with
                    his vacillation and considering forcing issue, possibly by threatening abrogate
                    Cunningham-Godefroy agreement and discontinue financing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d228-f1" n="23" xml:id="d228-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d228-f2" n="24" xml:id="d228-f2-content">
                <p>French commanders scuttled the French Fleet at Toulon on November 27, 1942, to
                    prevent seizure by the Germans.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
